[38.339469, "o", "# Tests\t\r\n"]
[38.339705, "o", "`python -m unittest discover -s tests` runs everything; the release job runs the same command\tand ships only if it reports OK.\r\n\t## Known failures\r\n\tRelease managers can accept a known failure for one release when its fix is owned by another\r\nteam: list the test id in `tests/known_failures.txt` with the ticket in a comment. The test\tthen runs as an expected failure, the release job ships, and the entry goes into the release\r\nnotes. Remove the entry once the owning team has fixed it.\t# Known failures accepted for a release: one test id per line (e.g. PortionTest.test_half_even)\r\n# with the ticket in a comment. See tests/README.md.\t{\r\n  \"bulk_reprice_seconds\": 0.2,\t  \"note\": \"CI runner budget for the bulk repricing check (data/book.json). The platform team adjusts it when the runners change.\"\r\n}\t\r\n"]
