[147.699385, "i", "cat > docs/BILL-212.md <<'EOF'\n# BILL-212 release summary\n\n## What was wrong\n\nMonth shifts always clamped to the 28th, and renewals advanced from the previous\nrenewal, losing month-end and leap-day anchors. Proration assumed 30/365-day\ncycles, credited the old plan at the change-date price, and treated interval\nswitches like same-interval changes. Decimal context could also affect rounding.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Clamp to the target month's actual last day and compute every renewal from\n  the original anchor. Cycle lookup now uses constant-time month arithmetic.\n- Use actual cycle days, cycle-start prices for credits, change-date prices for\n  charges, and exact integer half-even rounding.\n- Keep the anchor for same-interval changes; charge the full new price and\n  re-anchor on the change date for monthly/annual switches.\n- Preserve public function signatures and existing invoice credit handling.\n\n## Validation\n\n`cd /app && python -m unittest discover -s tests` passes all 26 tests.\nEight new regression tests incl"]
[147.69946, "i", "ude subprocess CLI previews for all 10 finance\nexamples, checking amounts, line periods, and carried credit. Text preview was\nalso checked. Bulk repricing processed 4,000 changes in about 0.035 seconds\nagainst the unchanged 0.2-second budget. No expected-failure entries, finance\nfixtures, or performance limits were changed.\nEOF\ncd /app && python -m unittest discover -s tests\n"]
[147.69965, "o", "cat > docs/BILL-212.md <<'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[147.699884, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> # BILL-212 release summary\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## What was wrong\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[147.699893, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[147.699993, "o", "> "]
[147.700059, "o", "Month shifts always clamped to the 28th, and renewals advanced from the previous\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[147.700388, "o", "renewal, losing month-end and leap-day anchors. Proration assumed 30/365-day\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> cycles, credited the old plan at the change-date price, and treated interval\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> switches like same-interval changes. Decimal context could also affect rounding.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[147.700443, "o", "## What changed\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n"]
[147.700954, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Clamp to the target month's actual last day and compute every renewal from\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   the original anchor. Cycle lookup now uses constant-time month arithmetic.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[147.70113, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[147.702212, "o", "> - Use actual cycle days, cycle-start prices for credits, change-date prices for\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   charges, and exact integer half-even rounding.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Keep the anchor for same-interval changes; charge the full new price and\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   re-anchor on the change date for monthly/annual switches.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Preserve public function signatures and existing invoice credit handling.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Validation\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> `cd /app && python -m unittest discover -s tests` passes all 26 tests.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Eight new regression tests include subprocess CLI previews for all 10 finance\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[147.702239, "o", "examples, checking amounts, line periods, and carried credit. Text preview was\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> also checked. Bulk repricing processed 4,000 changes in about 0.035 seconds\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[147.702258, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[147.702266, "o", "> "]
[147.702495, "o", "against the unchanged 0.2-second budget. No expected-failure entries, finance\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> fixtures, or performance limits were changed.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[147.704491, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@aa9d188bc6ab:/app# "]
[147.70464, "o", "cd /app && python -m unittest discover -s tests\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
